# Accepted Trivy findings for this repo's K8s manifests and the N1 capture
# image, caught by GitHub Advanced Security's repo-wide scan (the local
# `make check` / guardrails.yml static job only points trivy at infra/aws).
# Each ID below is a deliberate experiment-design choice, not an oversight.
# IDs verified against `trivy config gitops app/n1-capture` (CRITICAL,HIGH,MEDIUM).

# KSV-0044 "Role permits wildcard verb on wildcard resource"
# KSV-0112 "Role ... shouldn't manage all resources at the namespace"
# gitops/o1/baseline/rbac.yaml is the deliberately-permissive BEFORE state row
# O1 measures its least-privilege hardened RBAC against (ADR-0015, ADR-0019).
# Narrowing it would eliminate the thing the row proves.
KSV-0044
KSV-0112

# KSV-0049 "Role ... should not have access to resource 'configmaps' for
#   verbs [...]"
# KSV-0056 "Role ... should not have access to resources [...] for verbs [...]"
# gitops/o1/hardened/rbac.yaml's o1-controller Role is scoped with
# `resourceNames` to exactly one named object per rule (the one target pod,
# the one evidence configmap, the one release lease, the one quarantine
# NetworkPolicy) — as narrow as Kubernetes RBAC can express. These checks
# flag the verb+resource-type combination without crediting resourceNames
# scoping, so they fire on a Role that is already minimal by design.
KSV-0049
KSV-0056

# KSV-0009 "Deployment ... should not set hostNetwork to true"
# KSV-0118 "... is using the default security context, which allows root
#   privileges"
# KSV-0119 "... should not include 'NET_RAW' in securityContext.capabilities.add"
# DS-0002 "Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile with non-root user"
# gitops/n1/base/workload.yaml's n1-capture Deployment and its Dockerfile
# (app/n1-capture) are a tcpdump capture pod that has to see the node's real
# network interface to prove WireGuard encryption between nodes (ADR-0012):
# host networking and NET_RAW are the point, not a gap, and tcpdump needs
# root to open a raw socket. Same pattern as the netseg lab's Hubble capture.
KSV-0009
KSV-0118
KSV-0119
DS-0002
